# Identity keys, and nothing else.
#
# This project deliberately tracks build/ and run/ — that decision was made on
# purpose and reaffirmed, and this file is not a reversal of it. It is the one
# exception that decision never considered: these files are unencrypted PKCS#8
# private keys, and this repository is public.
#
# Three of them were published — the dedicated server's identity and the Alice
# and Bob dev identities — from `b1f35e7` until 2026-08-24. The server key was
# rotated, because it had signed nothing that survives: its market was deleted
# and the next start generates a new one. The two dev identities were not, and
# that is a decision rather than an oversight: they unlock nothing but make-
# believe markets in run/saves, and rotating them would make this machine a
# stranger to its own test worlds, since a second key for a registered user is
# refused by design.
#
# A private key in git history cannot be recalled. Rotating is what makes a
# published one worthless; this file is what stops the next one being published.
*.key
